\n\
Let me pass priority and get to postcombat main where I can play Glider Kids and a land.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually, I already have 3 untapped lands? Let me look at the board: Island, Island, Plains — First-Time Flyer is tapped (attacking). Wait, the board shows my lands as Island, Island, Plains with \"Untapped lands: 3\". Hmm, wait — I played Island on turn 1, Plains on turn 2, and on turn 3 I played... the summary said \"Island into Glider Kids\" but the board shows Glider Kids still in hand. So it seems I haven't played Glider Kids yet this turn. The log said I planned to but maybe I only attacked so far.\n\
\n\
Board: hand=[Airbender Ascension, Glider Kids, Momo, Playful Pet, Octopus Form, Plains], battlefield=[First-Time Flyer, Island, Island, Plains]. So I have 3 lands untapped. After combat I can play Plains and cast Glider Kids (2W) — that leaves one land untapped.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, I have 4 lands if I play Plains. Glider Kids costs {2}{W}, so I can cast it and have one Island left up for Octopus Form bluff? Actually Octopus Form costs {U} — I could keep an Island untapped.\n\
\n\
Should I use Octopus Form now? No — the flyer is unblocked, no reason. Save it for later as a protection spell.\n\
\n\
So: pass priority now, then postcombat play Plains, cast Glider Kids.\n\
\n\
