      "reasoning": "I'm in my postcombat main with 3 mana available. The best curve play is Glider Kids — a 2/3 flyer that keeps my air-pressure plan rolling and gives me a scry. Airbender Ascension is tempting, but developing a real threat matters more right now.",
      "thinking": "Let me analyze the situation. It's turn 3 postcombat main phase. I have:\n\
- Hand: Airbender Ascension, Glider Kids, Momo Playful Pet, Octopus Form, Plains\n\
- Battlefield: First-Time Flyer (1/2 flyer, tapped), Island, Island, Plains\n\
- 3 untapped lands, 0 land drops remaining\n\
\n\
Wait, I already played my land this turn (Island). So I have 3 lands total: 2 Islands, 1 Plains, all untapped except... wait, First-Time Flyer is tapped from attacking. My lands: Island, Island, Plains - all untapped it seems (3 untapped lands).\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
- Airbender Ascension {1}{W} - 2 mana\n\
- Glider Kids {2}{W} - 3 mana\n\
- Momo, Playful Pet {W} - 1 mana\n\
- Octopus Form {U} - 1 mana\n\
\n\
I have 3 mana (2 Islands, 1 Plains). I can cast Glider Kids ({2}{W}) which uses all my mana. That's the best curve play - a 2/3 flyer that scries 1.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, I could cast Airbender Ascension + Momo for 3 mana total. Airbender Ascension airbends a creature when it enters (up to one target creature - could target opponent's Rallier). Airbending exiles the creature and its owner can recast... actually airbend typically exiles and the owner can cast it for {2} or something. Let me think - in Avatar set, airbend exiles a creature and its owner may cast it from exile by paying {2} rather than its mana cost? Actually airbend: exile the creature, and its owner can cast it from exile for {2} (colorless) as long as it remains exiled. That's a tempo play.\n\
\n\
But Glider Kids is a solid 2/3 flyer which continues my aggressive air curve. My plan is aggressive flyers. The 2/3 body is great for blocking too.\n\
\n\
Airbender Ascension also triggers quest counters whenever a creature I control enters. Combined with Momo that's 2 counters (Ascension entering doesn't count itself? It says \"whenever a creature you control enters\" - when Ascension enters, it airbends a target creature. Then creatures entering after put counters).\n\
\n\
Actually, casting Ascension + Momo: Ascension ETB airbends (exile opponent's Rallier - but wait, \"airbend up to one target creature\" - airbending exiles until... the owner may cast for {2}). The opponent's Rallier is summoning sick and irrelevant anyway. Exiling it doesn't matter much - they can recast for 2.\n\
\n\
Hmm, but the tempo plan: I'm aggressive. Glider Kids is a 2/3 flyer which is exactly on curve. With First-Time Flyer already out, casting Glider Kids gives me two attackers next turn.\n\
\n\
Wait - actually First-Time Flyer gets +1/+1 if there's a Lesson in my graveyard. Octopus Form - is it a Lesson? It's {U} instant... Actually in Avatar set there are Lesson cards. Octopus Form might be a Lesson. Let me not worry.\n\
\n\
Best play: Cast Glider Kids for 3 mana. Simple, on curve, adds a 2/3 flyer, scry 1.\n\
\n\
Alternative: Momo (1/1 flying vigilance) + Ascension. That's 3 mana for a 1/1 flyer and an enchantment that airbends. The Ascension long-term value: after 4 creatures enter, blink a creature each end step. My creatures: First-Time Flyer ETB? None have great ETBs except Glider Kids (scry). Blinking Glider Kids gives scry 1. Not amazing.\n\
\n\
The aggressive line is Glider Kids. The opponent is at 19. I want pressure.\n\
\n\
Also consider: cast Momo + Ascension leaves opponent's Rallier exiled but recastable. Meh.\n\
\n\
I'll cast Glider Kids. Mana plan: tap both Islands and Plains? {2}{W} - use Plains for W, two Islands for generic. Auto-tap should handle it.",
