- Rallier can't block flyers.\n\
\n\
If they block Glider Kids with Glider Kids — mutual trade. Then First-Time Flyer gets in for 1. Opp goes to 18.\n\
\n\
Actually, would opponent trade their Glider Kids for mine? Possibly. Or they block the First-Time Flyer to save damage and keep their bigger body... Actually blocking the 1/2 kills a creature and they keep their 2/3 (now with 1 damage marked). That's probably better for them than trading 2/3 for 2/3.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, I hold back and play defensively? No — I'm the aggressive flying deck. But wait, what about my Octopus Form? I could attack, and if they block, cast Octopus Form on the blocked creature to save it (+1/+1 and hexproof until end of turn, untap). \n\
\n\
Scenario: Attack with both. Opp blocks my Glider Kids with theirs. I cast Octopus Form on my Glider Kids → it becomes 3/4 hexproof, deals 3 to their 2/3 (kills it), takes 2 damage and survives. That's a great trade for me! First-Time Flyer gets through for 1 (opp to 18).\n\
\n\
