      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "Combat situation: My First-Time Flyer (1/2) is blocked by their Glider Kids (2/3). My Glider Kids (2/3) is unblocked, going to hit them for 2.\n\
\n\
I have Octopus Form in hand: target creature I control gets +1/+1 and hexproof until end of turn, untap it.\n\
\n\
If I cast Octopus Form on First-Time Flyer, it becomes 2/3, still dies to Glider Kids (2/3)... wait, 2/3 vs 2/3: First-Time Flyer deals 2 to Glider Kids (3 toughness — survives with 2 damage marked). Glider Kids deals 2 to First-Time Flyer (3 toughness — survives). So both survive? Wait: First-Time Flyer becomes 1/2 + 1/+1 = 2/3. Glider Kids is 2/3. They trade damage: 2 damage each. First-Time Flyer has toughness 3, takes 2 — survives. Glider Kids has toughness 3, takes 2 — survives. So casting it on First-Time Flyer saves my creature and theirs too. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — without the pump, First-Time Flyer is 1/2. Blocked by 2/3 Glider Kids. First-Time Flyer deals 1 to Glider Kids (survives), Glider Kids deals 2 to First-Time Flyer (lethal, dies). So casting Octopus Form on First-Time Flyer saves it (1/2 → 2/3, survives 2 damage). That's worth it — save my flyer for one mana.\n\
\n\
Alternatively cast it on my unblocked Glider Kids to deal 3 instead of 2? That deals 3 damage to opponent, but loses my First-Time Flyer. Saving the First-Time Flyer is better — I keep a creature.\n\
\n\
The untap clause doesn't matter here much (First-Time Flyer is already... it's attacking, it's tapped, but untapping doesn't change combat status — it remains attacking).\n\
\n\
So: cast Octopus Form targeting First-Time Flyer to save it. Opponent's Glider Kids takes 2 and survives.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me reconsider — is there value in punishing? My creature survives either way with the form. The damage to their Glider Kids is 2 either way (power 2 after pump vs 1 before — wait, First-Time Flyer's power goes from 1 to 2, so it deals 2 damage to Glider Kids instead of 1). Still doesn't kill it (toughness 3).\n\
\n\
Hmm, but wait — First-Time Flyer gets +1/+1 if there's a Lesson in graveyard. No lessons.\n\
\n\
So decision: cast Octopus Form on First-Time Flyer. It survives, deals 2 to Glider Kids (which survives). My unblocked Glider Kids deals 2 to opponent (19 → 17).\n\
\n\
Alternatively, save the form for later use as a protection trick. But losing a 1/2 flyer to save a 1-mana instant seems bad. The card is meant for these situations. Also, hexproof is relevant protection.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think again about the math. First-Time Flyer blocked by Glider Kids 2/3. Without intervention: FTF dies, GK survives (takes 1). With Octopus Form on FTF: FTF becomes 2/3, deals 2 to GK, takes 2, both survive. So I save my creature at cost of one card. That's a good trade — my 1/2 flyer is worth more than the trick, and I've been curving well.\n\
\n\
Yes, cast it.",
