      "reasoning": "The Airbender Ascension ETB trigger is asking for an airbend target. Airbending their Water Tribe Rallier forces them to spend {2} to recast it — a nice tempo tax on their only creature and their card-advantage engine, and it can't block my flyers anyway. My First-Time Flyer is off-limits (it's a 3/4 hexproof beater until EOT), and airbending my own Glider Kids would just bench my attacker.",
      "thinking": "Airbender Ascension ETB: airbend up to one target creature. Airbending exiles a creature, and its owner can cast it for {2} generic rather than its mana cost? Actually airbend: exile target creature, and as long as it remains exiled, its owner may cast it for {2} instead of its mana cost. So airbending an opponent's creature lets them recast for 2. Hmm, but it's still removal-ish — they can recast Water Tribe Rallier for 2.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually in Avatar set, airbend: \"Exile it. For as long as that card remains exiled, its owner may cast it for {2} rather than its mana cost.\" So airbending opponent's 2/2 Rallier means they can recast for 2 — not great removal.\n\
\n\
