Actually wait — airbend text: \"its owner may cast it for {2}\" — I believe airbend in this set: \"Exile it. Until it... \" Let me check the oracle text to be sure. The reference doesn't define airbend. Let me quickly get oracle text. Actually, standard: \"Airbend a creature: Exile it. For as long as it remains exiled, its owner may cast it for {2} rather than its mana cost.\" That's the mechanic. Yes.\n\
\n\
So airbending Rallier = they can replay for 2. It's a tempo hit of 2 mana. Modest but positive. Airbending my Glider Kids = costs me 2 to replay, gains scry 1 and a quest counter. Actually that also advances my Ascension quest! Each creature entering puts a quest counter. If I recast Glider Kids, that's +1 counter. And Momo entering +1. And Water Tribe Captain +1.\n\
