\n\
Wait, combat already happened this turn (postcombat main). So Glider Kids already attacked. Next turn it untaps anyway. Airbending it and recasting for 2 next turn = scry 1 + quest counter + it's summoning sick. Meh.\n\
\n\
Their Rallier: it can't block my flyers. Is the tempo hit worth it? They'd recast it for 2, leaving 1 mana. Their turn 5: 4 lands presumably (they play a land). Recast Rallier (2), leaving 2-3 mana for other stuff. It does disrupt them somewhat. But honestly, airbending their creature that can't interact with my flyers seems low value. The Rallier's waterbend {5} is a mana sink — late game value. Denying that isn't critical.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually, is there any chance I want to NOT airbend? \"Up to one\" — I can decline. Airbending the Rallier gives them a \"free\" recast trigger? Rallier has no ETB. It just gives them flexibility. The main downside for them: 2 mana tax.\n\
\n\
Let me think about what maximizes my win rate: I'm racing in the air. They have no flying blocker currently (their Glider Kids died). Removing Rallier doesn't change combat. The 2-mana tax slows their development slightly. On the other hand, when they recast it, it returns with summoning sickness but same stats.\n\
\n\
I'd say airbend the Rallier — marginal tempo gain, no downside to me. Actually wait, there IS a consideration: if they recast the Rallier, does anything trigger? No.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, is there value in airbending my own creature to get quest counters faster? If I airbend Glider Kids now and recast it next turn along with Water Tribe Captain: turn 5 I'd have (assuming land drop) 5 mana. Recast Glider Kids (2) + Captain (3) = 5 mana, two creatures enter = 2 quest counters, plus Momo this turn = total 3 by end of turn 5. Then turn 6, one more creature = 4 counters → blink at end step.\n\
\n\
If I don't airbend Glider Kids: Momo (1 counter), turn 5 Captain (2 counters)... need 2 more creatures.\n\
\n\
The airbend-on-own-creature plan accelerates the quest but costs 2 mana and summoning sickness. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Actually, the Ascension end-step blink: \"exile up to one target creature you control, then return it\" — blinking Glider Kids = scry 1; blinking Momo = leaves-battlefield trigger (Food/+1/+1 counter/scry 2) AND it returns... wait, when Momo leaves, its trigger fires (choose one), and it returns to battlefield. Blink value is modest.\n\
\n\
I think the cleanest: airbend their Rallier for tempo. It's their only board presence. Even though it can't block flyers, keeping their board empty means if they want to develop, they pay the tax. Actually hmm — one more consideration: do they get to recast it immediately? They have 3 lands tapped... their lands are all tapped (they just played their turn? No wait — it's MY turn 4. Their lands are tapped from their turn 4 where they played Glider Kids which I killed, plus Rallier earlier. Their lands show tapped because they used mana on their turn and haven't untapped since — they'll untap on their turn 5.)\n\
