      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "Opponent is attacking with Otter-Penguin (3/2 with a +1/+1 counter... wait, it says 3/2 with 1 +1/+1 counter included, so actually it would be a 4/3? Wait: \"Otter-Penguin 3/2 (tapped, 1 +1/+1 counter, included in 3/2)\". So the 3/2 already includes the counter. Base is 2/1 + counter = 3/2. OK.\n\
\n\
They're attacking with Otter-Penguin (3/2) and Jeong Jeong's Deserters (1/2) into me at 20 life. I have blockers: Momo (1/1 flying vigilance) and Ally Token (1/1, summoning sick? No wait — blocking doesn't require being untapped... it requires being untapped, not non-sick. The token was created this turn but sickness only prevents attacking and tap abilities. Blocking is fine. Actually wait, it says Ally Token 1/1 (sick, token). Summoning sickness prevents attacking, not blocking. So it can block.\n\
\n\
Should I block? I'm at 20. They're attacking for 4 total (3+1). I could just take 4 and go to 16. But my board is much better than theirs — I'm at 20, they're at 11 with my air force. Do I want to trade my creatures?\n\
\n\
Momo blocks Otter-Penguin: Momo is 1/1, Otter-Penguin is 3/2. Momo dies, Otter-Penguin survives (takes 1). Bad trade — I lose Momo and don't kill theirs.\n\
\n\
Ally Token blocks Deserters: token 1/1 vs 1/2 — token dies, Deserters survive. Bad trade.\n\
\n\
Double-blocking Otter-Penguin with both: 1+1=2 damage to the 3/2, it survives. Both my creatures die. Terrible.\n\
\n\
So no blocks. Take 4, go to 16. They're at 11 facing my flyers (3/3 Flyer, 2/3 Glider Kids, 1/1 Momo) = 7 flying damage per turn. They're on a 2-turn clock (11 - 7 = 4, then dead). I'm at 16 facing 4 damage per turn on the ground. I win the race easily.\n\
\n\
No blocks. Take the 4.",
