Actually wait — what's my attack plan? Opponent's creatures are both tapped (Otter-Penguin and Deserters attacked last turn and are still tapped — meaning they don't have vigilance and will remain tapped until opponent's next untap step... wait, no. They attacked on opponent's turn 5, then it became my turn 6. Opponent's creatures untap at the beginning of their turn, so on my turn 6 they should be untapped... \n\
\n\
Hmm, wait. Let me re-read. The board shows Jeong Jeong's Deserters 1/2 (tapped) and Otter-Penguin 3/2 (tapped). It's my turn 6 precombat main. Opponent's creatures attacked on their turn 5, and then... their turn ended, my turn 6 began. Opponent's creatures stay tapped through my turn — they untap at the start of their next turn. Yes! That's correct. Creatures untap during their controller's untap step. So they're tapped during my whole turn 6.\n\
\n\
