      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "Let me assess the state. It's my turn 6, precombat main. The Equip ability targeting Momo is on the stack. I have priority.\n\
\n\
Board state:\n\
- Me (PilotA, 16 life): Airbender Ascension (3 quest counters), Ally Token 1/1, First-Time Flyer 3/3 (with Octopus Form lesson in graveyard giving +1/+1 — it says modified, 3/3), Glider Kids 2/3 flying, Kyoshi Battle Fan (equipping to Momo), Momo 1/1 flying vigilance (will become 2/1), Water Tribe Captain 3/3 (summoning sick). Lands: 3 Islands tapped, 2 Plains tapped. Hand: empty.\n\
\n\
Wait, First-Time Flyer is 1/2 base, +1/+1 from Lesson = 2/3, but it says 3/3. Hmm, it previously had Battle Fan equipped (+1/+0), so 3/3. Now I'm moving the Fan to Momo, so First-Time Flyer will be 2/3 after equip resolves.\n\
\n\
- Opponent (PilotB, 11 life): Barrels of Blasting Jelly, Jeong Jeong's Deserters 1/2 (tapped), Otter-Penguin 3/2 with +1/+1 counter (tapped). Lands: 2 Islands, Jasmine Dragon Tea Shop, Meditation Pools (tapped), North Pole Gates (tapped). No flying blockers. Hand: 1 card.\n\
\n\
Stack: my Equip {2} targeting Momo.\n\
\n\
I have priority with the equip on the stack. Nothing else to do — no hand, all lands tapped. I should pass priority, let equip resolve, then attack.\n\
\n\
Plan: Attack with everything that can attack: First-Time Flyer (will be 2/3), Glider Kids (2/3), Momo (2/1 vigilance), Ally Token (1/1). Water Tribe Captain is summoning sick, can't attack.\n\
\n\
Opponent has no flying blockers at all — Deserters and Otter-Penguin are ground creatures. So all my flyers get in unblocked. Damage: 2 + 2 + 2 = 6 in the air. Ally Token (1/1) could be blocked by... their creatures are tapped! Deserters and Otter-Penguin are both tapped, so they can't block at all. So Ally Token also gets in for 1. Total 7 damage. Opponent goes to 4.\n\
\n\
Wait, will they be tapped when I attack? They attacked on their turn 5, and it's my turn 6 — tapped creatures untap at the beginning of their controller's untap step, so they remain tapped during my turn. Yes, they can't block.\n\
\n\
So attack with First-Time Flyer, Glider Kids, Momo (vigilance, stays untapped), Ally Token. That's 2+2+2+1 = 7 damage. Opponent at 4.\n\
\n\
Should I hold back Momo? No — opponent at 11, going to 4. Kill next turn likely. Momo has vigilance so it stays untapped anyway. Attack with all four.\n\
\n\
Actually, should the Ally Token attack? Opponent's creatures are tapped, so no blockers. Free 1 damage. Yes.\n\
\n\
Pass priority now to let the equip resolve.",
