      "reasoning": "Momo died to Aang's flash block (Aang also airbent my First-Time Flyer into exile). With an empty hand, I'll take the Scry 2 mode on Momo's trigger to dig for more gas rather than a small power bump — I need to find finishers to close this out before their Barrels/Aang engine stabilizes.",
      "thinking": "Interesting! Something dramatic happened. Let me piece it together.\n\
\n\
I attacked with everything: First-Time Flyer (exiled??), Glider Kids, Ally Token, Momo... wait. The board shows:\n\
\n\
My battlefield: Airbender Ascension (quest=3), Ally Token 1/1 (tapped), Glider Kids 2/3 (tapped), Kyoshi Battle Fan, Water Tribe Captain 3/3 (sick), lands. Graveyard: Momo, Octopus Form. Exile: First-Time Flyer.\n\
\n\
Opponent: Aang, Swift Savior 2/3 (sick, copy of Aang and La, Ocean's Fury) — they flashed in Aang! Aang has flash and flying, and when it enters, airbend up to one other target creature or spell. They airbent my First-Time Flyer (it's in exile now — airbend exiles, and it can be recast for {2} generic... actually airbend: exile, and owner can cast it for {2}?). Airbend means the owner may cast the card from exile by paying {2} rather than its mana cost.\n\
\n\
Combat: Glider Kids is blocked by Aang (both 2/3, so they trade? Actually Glider Kids 2/3 vs Aang 2/3 — both deal 2 to each other, both would... 2 damage to a 2/3 = survives; 2 damage to Glider Kids 2/3 = survives. Both survive since each has toughness 3 and takes 2).\n\
\n\
Wait, but Momo is in my graveyard. Momo was equipped with the Battle Fan (2/1 flying vigilance). Aang has flash — opponent flashed in Aang and blocked... no wait, combat shows \"Glider Kids blocked by Aang\". Momo died somehow. Momo is 2/1 with the fan. Hmm, how did Momo die? Maybe blocked by Aang? No, combat shows Glider Kids blocked by Aang.\n\
\n\
Actually, maybe the opponent's Aang blocked Momo and then... no. Combat display: \"-> PilotB | Glider Kids -> PilotB | blocked by Aang, Swift Savior -> PilotB | Ally Token -> PilotB\". So there are multiple attackers; one was blocked by Aang. It's a bit garbled.\n\
\n\
