      "thinking": "I'm at postcombat main, turn 6. My hand is empty, but I have First-Time Flyer in exile — it was airbent by Aang. Airbend means the exiled card can be cast for {2}? Wait, let me think. Airbending exiles the card, and the owner can cast it from exile for {2} rather than its mana cost? Actually in this set, \"airbend\" exiles and lets the owner cast it by paying {2} generic. The choice shows First-Time Flyer [id=p4, cast, {1}{U}] — hmm, it shows {1}{U} which is its normal cost. But wait, my lands are all tapped (3 Islands tapped, 2 Plains tapped). I have 0 untapped mana. The choice says cast {1}{U} but I have no mana available...\n\
\n\
