\n\
Hmm, but the server says it's playable. Maybe airbend's cast-from-exile cost is {2} and something reduces it? Or maybe the server judges playability at cheapest cost and it can fail? The instructions said \"A cost that depends on the target or on a choice made while casting is judged at its cheapest, so such a spell can still fail to pay once you choose a target.\" But mana is mana — I literally have 0 available.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually maybe I misread. Let me recount: \"Island (tapped), Island (tapped), Island (tapped), Kyoshi Battle Fan, Plains (tapped), Plains (tapped)\". Yes, all 5 lands tapped.\n\
\n\
So casting First-Time Flyer would fail to pay. Best to just pass. Actually, could there be any reason to try casting? If it fails, maybe it just returns to choices. Not worth it. Actually, wait — maybe the server auto-taps? No, everything's tapped already.\n\
\n\
Actually, hold on. Maybe the airbend mechanic: \"exile it. The owner may cast that card for as long as it remains exiled, and they may spend mana as though it were mana of any color\" or costs {2} less? Regardless, I have no mana, so I can't cast it this turn.\n\
