3. Combat: attack with Glider Kids (2 in the air), maybe Captain and Ally on the ground? They have 4 ground blockers (Katara 3/3, Otter-Penguin 3/2, Deserters 1/2, Ally 1/1). If I send Captain + Ally: they block both, I trade Ally for something maybe, Captain trades with Katara. Hmm.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think: do I want to trade Captain for Katara? Katara can waterbend {X} to set base power/toughness — a big threat. Removing it is decent. But Captain is my anthem engine ({5}: team +1/+1). With 5 lands, next turn I could activate for 5... I have 5 lands, so next turn I have 6 mana if I draw/play a land. Hmm, no more lands in hand (hand is empty).\n\
\n\
Opponent at 8. Next turn: Glider Kids + First-Time Flyer both attack in the air (6 power in air with Fan equip... wait Fan is unattached; next turn I can equip for 2). Next turn air damage: Glider Kids 2 + First-Time Flyer 2 = 4, plus Fan +1 = 5 if equipped. If opponent at 6 after this turn, they die next turn unless they gain life or block.\n\
\n\
They have no flying blockers once Aang is exiled. Can they get Aang back? Only by removing my Iceberg. They have Barrels of Blasting Jelly ({5}, {T}, Sac: deal 5 to target creature) — that can kill a creature, not the enchantment. They could kill Glider Kids with it. Barrels is untapped! They have lands all tapped though, so can't activate {5} this turn.\n\
\n\
OK, main decision now: Iceberg target = Aang. That is clear. Exiling Aang also means if Iceberg leaves, Aang returns — but that's fine.\n\
\n\
Alternative targets: Katara (3/3 vigilance, their best ground creature) — but Aang is the only flying blocker and the flash threat; removing Aang guarantees air damage. Also Aang could transform with waterbend {8}. Exile Aang.\n\
\n\
Then choose_action with choice=\"p64\".\n\
\n\
Then the Ascension trigger resolves (quest counter 4). Then I still have precombat main — all lands tapped, nothing to cast (hand empty). Attack: Glider Kids in the air for sure. Ground: Captain and Ally — if they block, trades happen. Let me think about whether attacking with Captain is good.\n\
\n\
If I attack with Glider Kids, Captain, Ally:\n\
- Opponent blocks optimally: Katara blocks Captain (trade), Otter-Penguin blocks Ally (Ally dies), Deserters and Ally token... they have 4 blockers, I have 2 ground attackers. Ally token blocked by Otter-Penguin: token dies, penguin survives. Captain blocked by Katara: both die. Glider Kids unblocked: 2 damage → opponent at 6.\n\
- Result: I lose Captain and Ally token; they lose Katara. Then my board: Glider Kids, First-Time Flyer, Captain gone. Their board: Otter-Penguin, Deserters, Ally token, Barrels.\n\
\n\
Hmm, that weakens my board a lot. Alternatively attack with just Glider Kids: 2 damage, opponent at 6, keep everything back. Then next turn: attack with Glider Kids + First-Time Flyer (equip Fan to one): 2+1 + 2 = 5 or 6 in the air. If they don't remove a flyer, they die.\n\
\n\
But wait — opponent untaps next turn and can use Barrels ({5} sac: 5 damage to target creature) to kill one flyer. They have lands: Island x2, Jasmine Dragon Tea Shop, Meditation Pools, North Pole Gates = 5 lands. So they can activate Barrels to kill a flyer. Then I have the other flyer... they'd be at 6, one flyer attacks for 2-3 per turn. They also might waterbend Katara.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, keep pressure: maybe attack with Glider Kids only, keep Captain + Ally back. That seems safest.\n\
\n\
Actually, what about attacking with everything? Let me reconsider: if they block Katara on Captain — do they want to trade? Katara is their best card. They might block Captain with Otter-Penguin + Deserters instead: Captain (3/3) kills both? Captain deals 3: kills Penguin (3/2→2 toughness), deals 1 to Deserters (1/2), Captain takes 3 damage (2+1) and dies. That's a 2-for-1 in my favor! They'd prefer Katara blocks Captain. But Katara is sick (summoning sickness doesn't matter for blocking). Katara 3/3 vs Captain 3/3: trade. Would they trade Katara? They might, to avoid the 2-for-1.\n\
\n\
If they trade Katara for Captain, is that good for me? Katara's waterbend {X} is scary — with 5 lands they could make their team 4/4 or so. Removing Katara is valuable. And I keep Ally token... no wait, Ally token gets blocked by Penguin and dies.\n\
\n\
Hmm, or attack with Captain only + Glider Kids? Keep Ally back. Then: Katara blocks Captain (trade) or Penguin+Deserters double-block (I get 2-for-1). Either seems fine for me. If they just let Captain through (take 3), they go to 3 (2 from Glider + 3 from Captain = 5 damage; 8-5=3). Then next turn air attack kills.\n\
\n\
Wait, would they take 3 from Captain? They're at 8. If they take 5 total (2 air + 3 ground), they're at 3. Next turn I attack with Glider Kids + First-Time Flyer + Fan equip: 3+2=5 or so in the air — dead. So they must block. If they block Captain with Katara: trade. If double-block with Penguin+Deserters: I kill both, Captain dies. If they block with Ally token: token dies, Captain tramples? No trample — Captain just kills token and lives! Wait, Captain 3/3 vs Ally 1/1: Captain takes 1, survives as 3/2, token dies. That's bad for them. So they block with Katara (trade) or double-block.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — Katara is 3/3 sick; vigilance though. Blocking Captain: both 3/3, trade. They lose their best creature. If they double block Penguin + Deserters: lose both. If they let it through: at 3, dead next turn.\n\
\n\
So attacking with Captain + Glider Kids is great: worst case, trade Captain for Katara and opponent at 6; or get 2-for-1; or opponent at 3.\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, but what about their response... they have no untapped lands (all tapped), no cards in hand? Earlier said opponent has no cards in hand. So no tricks.\n\
\n\
Actually, hold on: does opponent have cards in hand? \"Opponent at 8 with no cards in hand\" from my earlier note. And they played Katara last turn. Let me trust that.\n\
\n\
Also the Ally token on their side is sick (summoning sick) — can't block? Summoning sickness prevents attacking and tap abilities, NOT blocking. It can block. But blocking Captain with a 1/1 is bad for them.\n\
\n\
So attack plan: Glider Kids + Water Tribe Captain (+ maybe Ally token). If I also send Ally token, they block it with Penguin or Deserters (token dies) — I'd rather keep the token? The token is a 1/1 that contributes to... it's an Ally. It can be equipped with Fan. Eh, keep it back — it chump-blocks Otter-Penguin on their swing back.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, let me reconsider: should I even attack with Captain? If they trade Katara for Captain, I lose my anthem engine. But board position: my flyers are the win condition; ground stall favors me since I win in the air. Trading Captain for Katara removes their waterbend threat. I think it's good.\n\
\n\
Hmm, alternatively, send everything: Captain, Ally, Glider Kids. They have 4 blockers (Katara, Penguin, Deserters, Ally). Optimal blocks for them: Katara on Captain (trade), Penguin on Ally (Ally dies). Glider through for 2. They keep Deserters + Ally token. Board after: me: 2 flyers; them: Penguin, Deserters, Ally token, Barrels. Opponent at 6.\n\
\n\
vs. sending Captain + Glider only: Katara on Captain (trade) — they keep Penguin, Deserters, Ally. Me: 2 flyers + Ally token. That's strictly better for me (I keep my token, they keep their ground guys but those don't matter much since I win in the air).\n\
\n\
So attack with Glider Kids and Water Tribe Captain only.\n\
\n\
But wait — actually, do I even want to trade Captain for Katara? What if I just attack with Glider Kids, keep Captain back? Opponent at 6. Then their turn: they can Barrels a flyer (kill Glider Kids, say). Then my air: First-Time Flyer 2/3 + Fan. Attack for 3/turn. They'd need to deal with it. They could also waterbend Katara to make blockers... Katara waterbend sets base P/T to X/X — doesn't grant flying. So they can never block flyers except with Aang (exiled) — unless they remove my Iceberg. Can they remove Iceberg? It's an enchantment. Their removal: Barrels (creature only), Aang (exiled), nothing else visible. They have 28 cards in library, no hand. So they can't easily remove Iceberg.\n\
\n\
So my air force is nearly unstoppable. The race: they swing on the ground. Their ground: Katara 3/3, Penguin 3/2, Deserters 1/2, Ally 1/1 = 8 power ground. My life: 16. My blockers: Captain 3/3, Ally 1/1 (flyers can block ground too: Glider Kids, First-Time Flyer — but I want to attack with them; flyers can block non-flying creatures).\n\
\n\
Given all this, attacking with Captain + Glider Kids seems optimal: forces the trade or big damage.\n\
\n\
Actually, one more consideration: the Ascension end-step trigger. At 4 counters, \"exile up to one target creature you control, then return it.\" Flicker Glider Kids → scry 1, quest counter 5. Good.\n\
\n\
But careful: if I flicker Glider Kids after combat, it returns untapped... fine.\n\
\n\
Also, should I flicker to \"reset\" something? First-Time Flyer has summoning sickness — flickering doesn't help (returns at end step, still can't attack until next turn anyway... actually flickering at end step means it comes back and next turn it's fine either way; First-Time Flyer was cast this turn, so next turn it's not sick regardless).\n\
\n\
OK so the immediate decision: target Aang with Iceberg ETB. Let me do that.\n\
\n\
