\n\
Actually let me think: If I attack with the 3/3 and they block, trade. Then next turn I attack with Glider Kids 2/3 unblocked → they go to 4, then 2, then 0. They draw cards each turn though.\n\
\n\
If they don't block, they go to 3. Then next turn I attack with both flyers (3/3 and 2/3) — they block one (4/3 blocks 3/3, trade... my 3/3 kills their 4/3 and dies? 3/3 vs 4/3: my creature takes 4 and dies, theirs takes 3 and dies. Trade). The 2/3 gets through → they're at 1. Then next turn the 2/3 attacks... they have no flyers. Dead.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, they also might have other blockers on the ground — but flyers can only be blocked by flyers/reach. Their only flyer is Geyser Leaper. So the air is clear except for the Leaper.\n\
\n\
Either way, attacking with First-Time Flyer is correct. Force the trade or get in for 3.\n\
\n\
Also should I attack with Glider Kids? No — it's summoning sick (just cast this turn). Can't attack.\n\
\n\
What about the Ally token? Did it survive? Let me recall: On turn 6 I attacked with everything; Momo died to Aang's block; \"my Glider Kids and Ally got through for 3\". The Ally token (2/1) got through. On turn 7, I held the Ally token back \"since they have enough ground blockers to kill it for free.\" So the Ally token is still around — 2/1. On turn 7 I attacked with Glider Kids and Water Tribe Captain. Captain traded with Otter-Penguin.\n\
\n\
So current board: First-Time Flyer 3/3 (with Fan), Glider Kids 2/3 (sick), Ally token 2/1, Airbender Ascension (6 counters after trigger resolves), Aang's Iceberg, 5 lands (tapped).\n\
\n\
Should I attack with the Ally token on the ground? Their ground: Geyser Leaper 4/3 can block on the ground too (it's a 4/3 flyer but can block ground creatures). If I send the 2/1 Ally, they block with Geyser Leaper 4/3, Ally dies free, Leaper survives (takes 2, has 3 toughness, survives with 1 toughness remaining... actually 2 damage to a 4/3 leaves it alive). That's bad — Ally dies for free.\n\
\n\
But if I send both First-Time Flyer (air) and Ally (ground), they can only block one with the Leaper. If they block the Ally, my 3/3 gets through for 3 → they go to 3. If they block the Flyer (trade), Ally gets through for 2 → they go to 4. Either way I get damage through! That's better.\n\
\n\
