      "thinking": "Let me analyze the combat situation:\n\
\n\
I'm at 16, opponent at 6. Their board:\n\
- Ally Token 1/1\n\
- Barrels of Blasting Jelly (artifact, not a creature)\n\
- Geyser Leaper 4/3 (sick, flying)\n\
- Jeong Jeong's Deserters 1/2\n\
\n\
My attackers available:\n\
- Ally Token 1/1\n\
- First-Time Flyer 3/3 (equipped with Battle Fan)\n\
- Glider Kids 2/3 is sick (just cast this turn), can't attack.\n\
\n\
Their flying blocker: Geyser Leaper 4/3. If I attack with First-Time Flyer 3/3, they block with Geyser Leaper 4/3 → my Flyer dies (3 damage to it) and I deal 3 to the Leaper... wait, Flyer is 3/3, Leaper is 4/3. Flyer deals 3 to Leaper (dies, 3 toughness), Leaper deals 4 to Flyer (dies). So they trade. That's bad for me — I trade my 3/3 flyer for their 4/3. Hmm, but actually opponent at 6 life. \n\
\n\
Ground: Deserters 1/2 and Ally token 1/1 can block my Ally token 1/1.\n\
\n\
If I attack with both: First-Time Flyer gets blocked by Geyser Leaper (trade), Ally token gets blocked by Deserters or their token (trade). That accomplishes nothing except trading.\n\
\n\
Alternative: don't attack, or attack with only the Ally token? No.\n\
\n\
Wait — think about this more. Opponent is at 6. My First-Time Flyer is 3/3. If unblocked, they go to 3. They will block with Geyser Leaper and trade. But trading my Flyer for their Leaper removes their only flying blocker, then my Glider Kids (2/3) is unopposed in the air next turns, dealing 2/turn. They're at 6 — that's 3 turns. Plus Ascension blink value.\n\
\n\
Actually, is the trade good? First-Time Flyer 3/3 for Geyser Leaper 4/3 — I think yes, because it clears the air for Glider Kids and the Ascension engine. But do I want to force it? If I attack, they choose to block. They might not block and take 3 (down to 3), preserving the Leaper. Either outcome is fine.\n\
\n\
Also the Ally token: attacking with it into Deserters 1/2 just trades 1/1 for 1/2? My 1/1 deals 1 to Deserters (doesn't kill 1/2... wait 1 damage to a 1/2 doesn't kill). Deserters deals 1 to my token, kills it. So attacking with the Ally token is strictly bad — it dies for free. Keep it back.\n\
\n\
So attack with First-Time Flyer only. If they block with Geyser Leaper, trade — my Glider Kids owns the sky afterward. If they don't block, they're at 3.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — should I consider not attacking at all and keeping the Flyer back as a blocker? Opponent's board: Geyser Leaper 4/3, Deserters, Ally token. They can attack for 4 in the air. I'm at 16, no danger. I'm way ahead. The race: I'm at 16, they're at 6. Glider Kids attacks for 2 each turn unopposed if Leaper is gone. \n\
\n\
I think attacking with First-Time Flyer is correct. The risk: they block with Leaper, trade. Fine. Or they take 3.\n\
\n\
Hmm, one more consideration: Barrels of Blasting Jelly — {5},{T},Sac: deal 5 to target creature. Their lands are all tapped now, but next turn they could have 5 mana to kill my Flyer. Attacking now forces the trade or damage before they can use Barrels. Actually if they want to kill my Flyer with Barrels, they can do it at instant speed on their turn regardless. Trading Flyer for Leaper now preempts that.\n\
\n\
Also, could attack with both Flyer and Ally token — token gets blocked by Deserters and dies for nothing. Bad. Just Flyer.\n\
\n\
Attack with First-Time Flyer only.",
