      "thinking": "Let me look at the combat situation. My First-Time Flyer (3/3) is blocked by their Geyser Leaper (4/3). Wait, actually the combat shows \"First-Time Flyer blocked by Geyser Leaper\". \n\
\n\
First-Time Flyer is 3/3, Geyser Leaper is 4/3. So Geyser Leaper deals 4 to my Flyer (killing it), and my Flyer deals 3 to Geyser Leaper (killing it). They trade. That's what opponent said — \"I'll take the trade here.\"\n\
\n\
My only available activation is Aang's Iceberg's Waterbend {3} sacrifice for scry 2 — but I have no mana (all tapped), so I can't even activate it. Wait, the choice says it's available... but Waterbend {3} requires {3} generic. Let me check my board: all my lands are tapped (3 Islands tapped, 2 Plains tapped). So how is the activation available? Waterbend allows tapping creatures to help pay? Actually waterbend is an ability where you can tap artifacts/creatures to pay. Hmm, but the exact rules here... The server says it's playable, so maybe I could tap creatures for it. But sacrificing Aang's Iceberg would release Aang, Swift Savior back to the battlefield — a flash flying 2/3 that could then airbend one of my creatures. That's terrible for me. Definitely not worth a scry 2.\n\
\n\
So I pass. The trade happens: First-Time Flyer and Geyser Leaper kill each other. That's fine — I still have Glider Kids 2/3 (will be untapped next turn), and opponent has no flying blockers left after Geyser Leaper dies. Opponent at 6.\n\
\n\
Pass priority.",
