\n\
Board state from memory:\n\
- Me: 16 life. Board: Glider Kids (2/3 flyer), Ally token (2/1), Airbender Ascension (6 quest counters), Aang's Iceberg (exiling their Aang, Swift Savior), Kyoshi Battle Fan (was attached to First-Time Flyer which just died, so now unattached). Lands: 5 (3 Islands, 2 Plains? Let me count: Island, Plains, Plains, Island, Island = 5 lands).\n\
- Opponent: 6 life. Board: North Pole Gates, lands (tapped), Barrels of Blasting Jelly, Aang exiled under my Iceberg. Geyser Leaper just died. 0 cards in hand.\n\
\n\
Wait, Aang, Swift Savior is a 2/3 flash flyer? Actually Aang, Swift Savior is a 2/3 flying creature with flash that when it enters, airbends up to one other target creature. Earlier they flashed it in, airbent my First-Time Flyer, blocked Momo. Then my Iceberg exiled it.\n\
\n\
Now it's my turn 8 postcombat main (after combat where Flyer and Geyser Leaper traded). I passed priority saying I won't sacrifice Iceberg. So I need to continue passing and see what happens next — likely my end step trigger of Ascension (at 6 quest counters, so it triggers at end step: blink a creature and reset counters... Actually let me recall Airbender Ascension's text.\n\
\n\
Airbender Ascension: Enchantment. When it enters, airbend target creature an opponent controls? Hmm, actually from the log: \"Airbender Ascension resolved and its ETB wants an airbend target. I'm airbending the opponent's Water Tribe Rallier.\" So ETB: airbend target creature. Then: \"Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a quest counter on this enchantment\" (or whenever you cast a creature spell? From the log it gained counters when creatures entered/resolved). At end step, if it has 4+ quest counters, exile it and return it to the battlefield? Actually: \"At the beginning of your end step, if this enchantment has four or more quest counters on it, exile up to one target creature you control, then return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control. Remove all quest counters from this enchantment.\"\n\
\n\
So at my end step, Ascension triggers (6 counters ≥ 4): blink a creature, remove counters.\n\
\n\
Also they have Barrels of Blasting Jelly: an artifact that taps and sacrifices to deal damage? \"Barrels of Blasting Jelly\" — probably {T}, sacrifice: deal 2 damage to target creature? Something like that. They were tapped out so couldn't activate.\n\
\n\
The instruction: \"Continue playing. Call pass_priority.\" So I call pass_priority and continue the loop.\n\
\n\
My plan: pass priority through postcombat main, then at end step, Ascension triggers — blink Glider Kids for scry 1 value (and it untaps as a blocker? it would return untapped). Then opponent's turn 8: they draw a card, maybe play something.\n\
\n\
