      "reasoning": "My end-step Ascension trigger is on the stack (7 quest counters). I'm blinking Glider Kids for the scry 1 ETB and another quest counter — the Battle Fan will detach, but I'll have plenty of mana to re-equip next turn, and the dig is free value with the opponent at 3.",
      "thinking": "End step of turn 9. Airbender Ascension trigger is on the stack (7 quest counters, so it fires). I need to choose a target creature to blink. Options: Ally Token (p54), Glider Kids (p84, equipped 3/3 flyer).\n\
\n\
Blinking Glider Kids gives me a scry 1 ETB, plus another quest counter. But wait — blinking would unequip the Kyoshi Battle Fan? No — equipment stays on the battlefield attached? When a creature leaves the battlefield, equipment stays on the battlefield but unattached. When Glider Kids returns, the Battle Fan would be unattached. That would remove the +1/+0 making it 2/3, and I'd need to re-equip for 2 mana. Not ideal, but I'd have untapped lands next turn.\n\
\n\
Actually, wait — do I need to choose a target at all? \"exile up to one target creature you control\" — it's \"up to one\", so I can choose not to target anything. The trigger is on the stack and I need to pick a target now.\n\
\n\
Blinking the Ally Token: tokens cease to exist when exiled, so the token wouldn't return. Bad.\n\
\n\
Blinking Glider Kids: returns, scry 1 trigger + quest counter trigger. The Battle Fan detaches. But I have Bender's Waterskin that untaps each player's turn — I can re-equip next turn if needed. The scry helps me dig. With opponent at 3, no flying blockers, lethal is basically locked up next turn regardless. Scry 1 helps me find something useful or bottom a land.\n\
\n\
Actually, there's a consideration: opponent's end-of-turn board — they have Barrels of Blasting Jelly with {5}, {T}, Sacrifice: deal 5 damage to target creature. It's tapped now, and they have limited untapped lands (Jasmine Dragon Tea Shop, Meditation Pools, Plains untapped — 3 mana available during my turn potentially). Not enough for the 5-cost activation during my turn (they'd need 5 mana; they have 3 untapped). On their next turn they'd have ~7 lands, could activate Barrels for 5 to kill my Glider Kids. But at 3 life facing a 3/3 flyer, they can't attack and must deal with it. Even if they kill it with Barrels, I have... hmm, that would cost them their turn and the Barrels.\n\
\n\
Anyway — the target choice: Glider Kids for scry 1 seems right. The unequip is a minor cost. Alternatively, target nothing and keep the Fan attached. But the blink also gives a quest counter which is irrelevant. The scry 1 is the main value. Since lethal is nearly guaranteed, scry is marginal, but free value is free value. Also blinking Glider Kids untaps it — it's currently tapped from attacking. Untapped blocker doesn't matter much since opponent won't attack into me... actually they might attack to force blocks? No, attacking into my 3/3 flyer with ground creatures does nothing.\n\
\n\
Wait, one more consideration: if I blink Glider Kids, Battle Fan detaches. Glider Kids returns as a 2/3 (base 2/3). Hmm, actually it returned to 2/3, and I'd need to re-equip for 2 to make it 3/3. Next turn I'll have 5 lands + Waterskin = 6 mana, plenty to re-equip for 2. Fine.\n\
\n\
Actually, should I blink the Ally Token instead to avoid detaching? No — token gets exiled and doesn't come back (tokens cease to exist as a state-based action before the return happens; the delayed trigger can't return it). So that loses the token.\n\
\n\
Choose Glider Kids (p84).",
