      "thinking": "The scry 1 revealed First-Time Flyer. Opponent is at 3 life with an empty-ish board (1 card in hand). I have Glider Kids equipped... wait, the Fan detached when Glider Kids was blinked. Glider Kids is 2/3 sick (just returned from blink).\n\
\n\
Opponent at 3 life, their board: Ally token 1/1, Jeong Jeong's Deserters 1/2, Water Tribe Rallier 2/2 (sick). No flying blockers. Their Aang is exiled under my Iceberg.\n\
\n\
If I keep First-Time Flyer on top, I draw it next turn. Then I can cast it (Ascension trigger), and attack with First-Time Flyer + Glider Kids in the air. First-Time Flyer would be 1/2 base, +1/+1 for Lesson in graveyard = 2/3. That plus Glider Kids 2/3 (or re-equip Fan for 3/3) — lethal.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me think: next turn I have 6 lands + Bender's Waterskin (untaps on my turn too... actually it untaps during each other player's untap step, and presumably my untap step as normal). So I'll have ~7 mana. Draw First-Time Flyer, cast it ({1}{U}), then re-equip Fan to Glider Kids ({2}), and attack: First-Time Flyer 2/3 flying (Lesson in gy) + Glider Kids 3/3 flying = 5 damage in the air, opponent at 3 with no flying blockers = lethal.\n\
\n\
Even without First-Time Flyer: Glider Kids 3/3 alone = 3 damage = lethal. So I don't even need First-Time Flyer for the win. But keeping it gives redundancy — if opponent somehow removes Glider Kids, I need another attacker. With an empty hand otherwise, topdecking First-Time Flyer gives me a body. It's definitely worth keeping on top over bottoming.\n\
\n\
Bottom the land cards; keep creatures. First-Time Flyer is a creature = action. Keep on top.\n\
\n\
So the choice: select up to one card to put on the bottom. To keep on top, I choose \"no\" (put nothing on bottom).\n\
\n\
Wait, the message says \"Select up to one card to PUT on the BOTTOM of your library (Scry)\". Choices: First-Time Flyer [id=p103]. Respond: choice=pN, or choice=no to cancel.\n\
\n\
So choosing \"no\" = keep on top. Yes, that's what I want — keep First-Time Flyer on top to draw next turn.",
