One more consideration: opponent's Water Tribe Rallier has Waterbend {5} to dig for a creature. They have 7 lands (6 tapped + 1 Plains). On their turn they untap and could activate Rallier's waterbend {5} to find a creature (power 3 or less). They might find a flyer or something. But nothing I can do about that. They're at 3 — if they don't find an answer, they die to my 3/3 flyer.\n\
\n\
Also note: they have 1 card in hand. Could be a removal for my Flyer. If they kill the Flyer, I still have Ascension generating blinks and... my board would be just an Ally token. My library: 24 cards. I draw each turn. Fine.\n\
\n\
Also, should I equip now or wait until next turn? If I equip now and they have an instant-speed kill spell, they kill the Flyer and the Fan stays (equipment survives). If I wait until next turn to equip, same thing. Equipping now is fine and frees up mana thinking. Actually — one reason to wait: keep mana up for... I have no instants in hand (hand is empty). So no reason to keep mana up. Equip now.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually there's a subtle point — should I equip BEFORE the Ascension end-step trigger? If I equip now, and then at end step Ascension's trigger... I choose not to blink. Fine.\n\
\n\
But hmm, what if I blink the Ally token... no, it dies. Don't.\n\
\n\
OK so right now: pass priority (choice=no) since the only option is the Iceberg activation which I don't want. Then the trigger resolves and I should get another shot to act — hopefully the Equip option appears.\n\
\n\
Let me also send a chat message at some point — haven't chatted in a while per the instructions. Let me do that alongside.\n\
\n\
Let me pass now.",
