      "reasoning": "The equip resolved — First-Time Flyer is now a 3/3 flyer with the Battle Fan, and the opponent is at 3 life with zero flying blockers (Aang still exiled under my Iceberg). My only options are re-equipping to the same creature (pointless) or sacrificing Aang's Iceberg (releases Aang — a hard no). Passing to end step, where Ascension's trigger will blink my Ally token for a free quest counter while keeping the Fan attached.",
      "thinking": "The equip is already done. I have an Island untapped and the Waterskin. My only plays are Iceberg sacrifice (releases Aang — no) or... wait, I already equipped the Fan this turn? The Battle Fan shows as a choice \"activate\" — but I equipped it to First-Time Flyer already. Actually it seems the equip activation is available again? But I don't have 2 mana — I have 1 Island + Waterskin... wait Waterskin isn't shown as usable for the equip cost? Equip {2} costs 2 generic; I have 1 Island + Waterskin = 2 mana. Hmm, but I already equipped to First-Time Flyer this turn — re-equipping to the same creature is pointless.\n\
\n\
Wait, actually looking at the board: First-Time Flyer 3/3 with... Kyoshi Battle Fan listed separately in my battlefield list. The Flyer is 3/3 (which is base 2/2 + 1 from Lesson? No — base is 1/2, +1/+1 from Lesson = 2/3, +1/+0 from Fan = 3/3). The board shows \"First-Time Flyer 3/3 (sick)\" so the Fan is attached. The choice to activate Equip again would just re-attach it to the same creature for no benefit. Don't waste mana — keep the Island up? Actually there's nothing to bluff; but no reason to spend 2 mana re-equipping to the same creature. Equip to Ally token? No benefit — the Flyer is my lethal threat.\n\
\n\
Pass to end step. Ascension at 9 counters will blink something. I'll blink First-Time Flyer? That would detach the Fan and make it sick again — bad, it can't attack next turn... wait, blinking at end step means it returns immediately, and on my next turn it won't be summoning sick (it entered before my turn begins... actually no — creatures that enter during my end step ARE able to attack next turn since they're under my control at the start of my turn? A creature needs to have been under my control continuously since the beginning of my most recent turn. If it returns during my end step, then at the start of my next turn it has been under my control since before that turn began, so it can attack). Yes — blinked at end step, returns immediately, can attack next turn.\n\
\n\
But blinking the Flyer detaches the Fan, and I'd need to re-equip. I have Island + Waterskin now... if I blink the Flyer, Fan falls off, and next turn I can re-equip with 6 mana. Alternatively blink the Ally token — no ETB, pointless but keeps everything else intact. Actually blinking the Ally token still adds a quest counter. Or blink nothing (\"up to one\"). \n\
\n\
Best: blink the Ally token? No benefit except a counter. Or blink First-Time Flyer — no ETB on Flyer, detaches Fan (need 2 mana to re-equip next turn, fine with 6 lands + Waterskin). Hmm, actually no reason to blink the Flyer. Blink the Ally token for a free quest counter, keeping Fan attached and mana available. Actually wait — should I use the equip NOW to... no.\n\
\n\
Actually, consider: I could blink the Flyer and re-equip postcombat now? I only have 1 Island + Waterskin untapped = 2 mana, exactly equip cost. But the blink happens at end step trigger, which is after postcombat main. Can't equip after end step (sorcery speed). So no.\n\
\n\
Simplest: pass to end step, blink the Ally token (quest counter to 10), keep Fan on the 3/3 Flyer. Next turn attack with Flyer (3/3) and Ally (1/1) for lethal — opponent has no flying blockers. Even the Flyer alone is exactly 3 = lethal.\n\
\n\
Pass now.",
