\n\
Or if I decline the blink: flyer stays tapped with Fan attached; turn 12 it untaps, attack for lethal. Either way works. Declining keeps Fan attached — simpler and saves {2}. But blinking gives a quest counter (irrelevant) and untapped blocker on their turn (they have no flying attackers; their ground attackers are irrelevant at 13 life). I'll probably decline again... actually wait — one consideration: if I blink the First-Time Flyer, it re-enters and triggers Ascension (quest counter) and... no other ETB. And it would be a fresh 3/3 (with Lesson) but Fan detached — becomes 2/3... wait no: First-Time Flyer base is 1/2, +1/+1 from Lesson = 2/3, +1/+0 from Fan = 3/3. Without Fan: 2/3. With re-equip: 3/3.\n\
\n\
Decision at that point: decline blink probably, keep the 3/3 intact and untap next turn for lethal.\n\
\n\
