But wait — North Pole Patrol has \"Waterbend {3}, {T}: Tap target creature an opponent controls.\" They have two Patrols now. On my turn, they could tap my First-Time Flyer before combat to prevent the lethal attack! The Patrol that's untapped (2/3, not sick) — its ability requires {T}, so it can activate (it was played last turn or earlier? It says North Pole Patrol 2/3 without \"sick\", so it can tap). Waterbend {3} — they have mana: Island untapped, Kyoshi Village untapped, Plains x2 untapped = 4 mana sources. Waterbend {3} means paying 3 extra... actually waterbend is an additional cost that can be paid by tapping creatures/artifacts? Waterbend lets you pay by tapping untapped artifacts/creatures you control, each contributing {1}. They have tapped creatures though. Their untapped stuff: Island, Kyoshi Village, Plains, Plains = 4 lands, plus North Pole Patrol itself can be tapped as part of waterbend? Actually waterbend: \"You may tap an untapped artifact or creature you control rather than pay {1} for each...\" Hmm, but the Patrol's own {T} cost can't be paid if it's tapped for waterbend... actually a creature can't be tapped both for its own {T} cost and for waterbend. So they need 3 mana from lands/creatures plus the Patrol untapped for the {T}.\n\
\n\
They have 4 untapped lands (Island, Kyoshi Village, 2 Plains). So yes, they can activate Patrol's waterbend {3}, {T} to tap my First-Time Flyer on my turn before combat. That would fizzle my lethal attack.\n\
\n\
Hmm. But that's on their turn/next turn. Right now my only choice is Iceberg sacrifice (releases Aang — bad) or pass. Pass.\n\
\n\
