Wait, actually — I need to be careful here. In Magic's CURRENT rules, tapping an attacking creature does NOT remove it from combat. This was changed way back (6th edition rules, 1999). Under modern rules, a creature that becomes tapped after being declared as an attacker remains an attacking creature and deals combat damage normally. Tapping only prevents a creature from BEING DECLARED as an attacker.\n\
\n\
So North Pole Patrol's ability \"tap target creature an opponent controls\" — to prevent my Flyer from attacking, they must tap it BEFORE I declare attackers, i.e., during my precombat main phase or upkeep. Once I've declared it as an attacker, tapping does nothing.\n\
