      "reasoning": "My 3/3 First-Time Flyer is already declared as an attacker, and they have zero flying blockers — even if they spend Waterbend {3} to tap it now, it's already in combat and tapping doesn't remove it. The 3 damage is guaranteed lethal. Passing priority to let combat resolve.",
      "thinking": "The opponent has 0 cards in hand and 3 life. If they activate it, my First-Time Flyer gets tapped... but wait, I already declared attackers. Tapping an already-attacking creature does NOT remove it from combat. So even if they tap my Flyer, it still deals combat damage.\n\
