\n\
So the main candidates: Airbender Ascension (13), Sokka's Haiku (11), Otter-Penguin (2), Barrels of Blasting Jelly (6), Rumble Arena (5).\n\
\n\
The deck is UW flyers/allies with card draw synergy. Airbender Ascension is a rare that fits perfectly - airbend removes an opposing creature temporarily, and with lots of creatures entering (tokens from Katara, Kyoshi Battle Fan, etc.), quest counters build up. Having two copies is strong.\n\
\n\
Sokka's Haiku is a counterspell that cantrips, mills (synergy with Lessons), and untaps a land - effectively costs 3 if you untap a land. Actually \"untap target land\" means net cost is 4 mana effectively... it costs {3}{U}{U} and untaps one land, so effectively {2}{U}{U}... still heavy blue. The deck has Tiger-Seal, Waterbending Lessons, First-Time Flyers - blue is well supported. This is a solid card.\n\
\n\
But Airbender Ascension at 1W is a cheaper, on-color rare that we know works. We already have one - doubling up on a good rare is great.\n\
\n\
